                <pb facs="0418" n="410" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg410"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/1621a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Consul at
                        Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Butrick</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-07-31T18:00:00-04:00">July 31, 1940—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>335. Wireless to the <hi rendition="#italic">New York Times</hi> under Shanghai
                    date line July 31 contains a statement that “it was reported that several of the
                    Japanese agency offices in Shanghai late yesterday received cabled orders from
                    the head offices in Tokyo to stress anti-American features in news items from
                    China”.</p>
                <p>The Department would appreciate receiving by radio such pertinent information
                    with regard to this statement as you may be able readily to obtain, together
                    with your comment with regard thereto.</p>
                <p>Sent to Shanghai. Repeated to Peiping and Chungking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
